    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0365" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.85/35</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-26T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 26, 1918,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 26, 5.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 20, 2 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d476-f1"/> Steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Penza</hi> has resumed regular journeys between
                    Vladivostok and Shanghai and is under no control by the Chinese Government save
                    for a special passport control exercised by the local authorities while within
                    Chinese territorial waters. I am so informing consulate at Vladivostok.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
